1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,914
This walkthrough configures the Data tab
for one first-level run from OpenNeuro

2
00:00:05,914 --> 00:00:07,885
dataset ds005085, participant sub-10015.

3
00:00:07,885 --> 00:00:13,799
Before entering values in FEAT, use the
terminal to inspect the exact

4
00:00:13,799 --> 00:00:15,278
four-dimensional BOLD image.

5
00:00:15,278 --> 00:00:20,206
`fslval` reports 260 volumes and a
repetition time of 1.

6
00:00:20,206 --> 00:00:21,192
7 seconds.

7
00:00:21,192 --> 00:00:25,627
The image dimensions are 86 by 86 by 51.

8
00:00:25,627 --> 00:00:32,527
These header values are evidence; a
remembered value or a value left over from

9
00:00:32,527 --> 00:00:34,991
another FEAT session is not.

10
00:00:34,991 --> 00:00:37,455
The modeled run is
`sub-10015_task-sharedreward_acq-mb3me1_bo

11
00:00:37,455 --> 00:00:37,948
ld.

12
00:00:37,948 --> 00:00:38,441
nii.

13
00:00:38,441 --> 00:00:38,934
gz`.

14
00:00:38,934 --> 00:00:42,384
Confirm all BIDS entities in the filename.

15
00:00:42,384 --> 00:00:48,791
Similar runs can sit beside each other,
and selecting the wrong echo or

16
00:00:48,791 --> 00:00:54,212
acquisition can still produce a
technically valid analysis of the wrong

17
00:00:54,212 --> 00:00:54,705
data.

18
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:59,087
In FEAT, select First-level analysis and
Full analysis.

19
00:00:59,087 --> 00:01:02,177
Set the number of inputs to one.

20
00:01:02,177 --> 00:01:05,709
This model represents one run from one
participant.

21
00:01:05,709 --> 00:01:11,890
It should not be named or interpreted as a
subject-level combination or a group

22
00:01:11,890 --> 00:01:12,331
result.

23
00:01:12,331 --> 00:01:16,305
Choose the verified BOLD file as the
four-dimensional input.

24
00:01:16,305 --> 00:01:22,044
Do not select the JSON sidecar, a mean
functional image, or a three-dimensional

25
00:01:22,044 --> 00:01:22,927
example volume.

26
00:01:22,927 --> 00:01:27,342
Once the path appears, compare its
participant, task, and acquisition

27
00:01:27,342 --> 00:01:31,316
entities with the run named in the
analysis notes.

28
00:01:32,166 --> 00:01:34,246
Set the TR to 1.

29
00:01:34,246 --> 00:01:37,989
7 seconds and the number of volumes to
260.

30
00:01:37,989 --> 00:01:41,317
Together those values imply a 442-second
time series.

31
00:01:41,317 --> 00:01:47,141
That duration gives us a useful boundary
check for every event onset loaded later.

32
00:01:47,141 --> 00:01:53,380
If a timing row falls beyond the run, stop
and repair the timing inputs before

33
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:54,628
fitting the model.

34
00:01:54,628 --> 00:02:00,036
Set deleted volumes to zero for this
course example because the supplied run

35
00:02:00,036 --> 00:02:03,364
and timing files are being modeled as
staged.

36
00:02:03,364 --> 00:02:07,524
For another dataset, non-steady-state
handling must come from the acquisition

37
00:02:07,524 --> 00:02:11,267
and preprocessing record rather than
imitation of this value.

38
00:02:12,117 --> 00:02:15,033
Set the output path to
`/home/jovyan/Voxelwise-Walkthroughs/outpu

39
00:02:15,033 --> 00:02:16,005
ts/sub-10015_sharedreward_mb3me1_L1_video`
.

40
00:02:16,005 --> 00:02:17,948
FEAT will append `.

41
00:02:17,948 --> 00:02:18,434
feat`.

42
00:02:18,434 --> 00:02:23,779
The name captures participant, task,
acquisition, level, and this recorded run

43
00:02:23,779 --> 00:02:27,666
while remaining independent of the source
data directory.

44
00:02:27,666 --> 00:02:34,468
Before leaving the tab, read the input
path, TR, volume count, and output path

45
00:02:34,468 --> 00:02:34,954
aloud.

46
00:02:34,954 --> 00:02:38,841
Confirm that the output does not already
exist.

47
00:02:38,841 --> 00:02:41,757
Save the design as a checkpoint.

48
00:02:41,757 --> 00:02:49,531
The Data tab is complete only when those
values agree with the image header and the

49
00:02:49,531 --> 00:02:51,475
planned unit of analysis.
